{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DominanceWellFounded","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Sigma.Lex"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.murphyLex_induction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.murphyLex_induction","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyInductionMeasure.lean#L114-L122","doc":"**The recursor an induction proving 3.14 would use.**  To prove `C` at a\nshape-and-tabloid, it suffices to prove it given `C` at every pair that is either of\nlex-greater shape, or of the same shape with a strictly dominating tabloid — which are\nexactly 3.14's cases (i) and (ii). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.instIsWellFoundedMurphyLex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.instIsWellFoundedMurphyLex","kind":"instance","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyInductionMeasure.lean#L110-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.murphyLex_wellFounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.murphyLex_wellFounded","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyInductionMeasure.lean#L104-L108","doc":"**Mathas 3.14's induction measure is well-founded.**  A strict order on a finite type;\nthe type is finite because there are finitely many shapes of size `n` and finitely many\ntabloids of each. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.instIsTransMurphyLex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.instIsTransMurphyLex","kind":"instance","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyInductionMeasure.lean#L91-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.instIsIrreflMurphyLex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.instIsIrreflMurphyLex","kind":"instance","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyInductionMeasure.lean#L85-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.murphyLex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.murphyLex","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyInductionMeasure.lean#L81-L83","doc":"**3.14's induction measure**: lex on shapes, dominance inside a shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.ShapedTabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyInductionMeasure.ShapedTabloid","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyInductionMeasure.lean#L77-L79","doc":"A shape of size `n` together with a tabloid of that shape — the object 3.14's double\ninduction runs on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}